  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader in light mode, I want the header of an ordinary quote (\"X a écrit\", `b.s1`) in an allowlisted message of the classic look at 4.5:1 or more, so that it stays readable. #644 (PR #1355) fixed the folded blocked quote header there; the ordinary one was left out.\n\n### Facts\n- `--secondary` on the classic allowlist surface (`--love`, light) is 4.45:1 (the #644 figure); `reader.css` raises only `table.quote-blocked b.s1` there. Not asserted by any test today (found by the Opus review of the #1360 PR, which reads the element in its probe).\n\n### Scope\nExtend the `.message.whitelist` rule of #644 to the ordinary quote header (`--secondary-tinted`), and assert it in `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests` (index 3 of the probe), failing before the change; check modern too.\n\n### Acceptance\n≥ 4.5:1 light and dark, both looks, no other contrast test regresses.\n\nFound by: Opus review of the #1360 PR (cloud/i1358-sonnet).",
